# The SuperCred runner image builds with the REPO ROOT as its context, because
# its Dockerfile COPYs manifests and scripts from all over the tree. That makes
# every stray directory at the root part of the build context, and one of them
# is not readable by the user running docker:
#
#   .cache/zot   drwxr-x---  65532:65532   <- created by the in-cluster zot
#
# The daemon tars the context before it looks at the Dockerfile, so a directory
# it cannot stat fails the build outright, before a single COPY is evaluated:
#
#   checking context: can't stat '/home/andy/src/cp/osramp-demo/.cache/zot'
#   FAILED: docker build failed for supercred-demo-runner:local
#
# Nothing here is ever COPYed into an image. Excluding it also stops the context
# tar carrying build state, dependency trees and git history it has no use for.
.cache/
.git/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
worktrees/
.worktrees/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
.keys/
